Fish Speech is pinned to commit 541566932abbaebcb0a40e562a1f846738383f38.
Drama 3 Studio modifies its Drama 3 generator and audio-tower sampler so that
top_k=0 disables top-k truncation while preserving top-p sampling.
The modifications are recorded in third_party/fish-speech.patch.
The Fish Audio Community License is included in licenses/fish-audio/LICENSE.
`src/drama_low_vram/data/control-head.safetensors` contains the unchanged
`<|audio_separator|>` output row extracted from the official Drama 3 output
head. It is bundled as a small runtime support file for the downloaded Comfy
quantized variants; the model weights remain separate downloads.

The native backend includes modifications to audio.cpp, pinned to commit
624cf918e51263d39c2a0d28a6c5e3d55990b79f, and uses ggml.
Their notices and license terms are included in licenses/audio-cpp/LICENSE
and licenses/ggml/LICENSE. The native modifications are recorded in
native/audio-cpp-runtime.patch.

The bundled script editor uses CodeMirror, Lucide and their dependencies.
Their copyright notices and license texts are retained in ui/licenses/.

The project mark is a rounded shark silhouette built from audio waveform bars
and supplied by the project author.
